<title>HONG KONG: HK still Taiwan's biggest air cargo partner in Dec.</title>
<headline>HK still Taiwan's biggest air cargo partner in Dec.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan remained Hong Kong's leading trading partner for both air cargo imports and exports during December 1996, Civil Aviation Department statistics show.</p>
<p>Most flights are to the capital Taipei but the southern Taiwanese city of Kaohsiung also featured in the top 20 list of imports of mainly belly cargo on airlines such as Hong Kong Dragon Airlines.</p>
<p>Reflecting strong pre-Christmas trade with Japan, Tokyo's Narita airport was in second place for both air cargo loaded and unloaded at Hong Kong's Kai Tak airport, the statistics show.</p>
<p>The level of air cargo exports from Hong Kong show an overall decrease during December as the bulk of shipments had already been made during the height of the pre-Christmas peak season in November, industry sources said. December 1996's top 20 origins for imports into Hong Kong by scheduled operators in tonnes:</p>
